.TH TTYCHATTER.MAILBOT 1 "June 2026" "ttychatter.mailbot 0.6.4-ai-file-receipt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ttychatter.mailbot \- email transport adapter and remote control surface for ttychatter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--config-file PATH] [--once|--daemon] [--dry-run] [--open-to-public]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--doctor] [--list-candidates] [--cleanup-public-sessions]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--config|--raw-config] [--sessions|--list-sessions] [--manpage]
[--model-cache] [--model-search TEXT] [--search TEXT|--search-sessions TEXT]
[--update-models] [--rename-session SESSION TITLE] [--delete-session SESSION]
[--turns SESSION] [--branch SESSION TURN] [--export SESSION --format FORMAT]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--ttychatter-backend python|c|bash|auto|command]
[--ttychatter-command COMMAND] [--ttychatter-extra-args ARGS]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--set KEY VALUE] [--unset KEY] [--set-imap-password [--gpg]]
[--set-smtp-password [--gpg]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ttychatter.mailbot reads unread IMAP mail, maps each accepted message to a
chat session or an allowlisted control command, invokes a ttychatter client,
and replies by sendmail or SMTP.
.PP
The mailbot is a transport adapter. It does not contain OpenRouter chat logic.
The selected ttychatter backend owns model calls, context reconstruction,
session logs, attachments, model selection, and exports.
.PP
The default backend remains
.B ttychatter.python
for existing deployments. The same mailbot can now use the current C CLI or the
Bash-only client by setting TTYCHATTER_BACKEND or TTYCHATTER_COMMAND.
.SH BACKENDS
.TP
.B TTYCHATTER_BACKEND=python
Use
.B ttychatter.python
(default).
.TP
.B TTYCHATTER_BACKEND=c
Use the C CLI command
.B ttychatter.
.TP
.B TTYCHATTER_BACKEND=bash
Use
.B ttychatter.bash.
.TP
.B TTYCHATTER_BACKEND=auto
Use the first available command in this order: ttychatter, ttychatter.python,
ttychatter.bash.
.TP
.B TTYCHATTER_BACKEND=command
Use TTYCHATTER_COMMAND exactly.
.TP
.B TTYCHATTER_CLIENT=python|c|bash|auto|command
Legacy alias for TTYCHATTER_BACKEND. New configs should prefer TTYCHATTER_BACKEND.
.TP
.B TTYCHATTER_COMMAND=COMMAND
Override the backend map. COMMAND is split with shell-like quoting.
.TP
.B TTYCHATTER_EXTRA_ARGS=ARGS
Extra arguments added to chat subprocesses. This is commonly used for local
smoke tests, for example ARGS="--demo".
.PP
Chat calls use the current cross-backend form:
.PP
.RS
.nf
COMMAND [TTYCHATTER_EXTRA_ARGS] --loopback --input - --attach FILE --session PATH
.fi
.RE
.PP
This works with the current C version, ttychatter.python, and ttychatter.bash.
.SH PRIVATE SUBJECT GRAMMAR
.TP
.B ordinary email subject
Send the message body to this sender's private subject-named session when
SUBJECT_SESSIONS=1. Reply prefixes such as Re: and Fwd: are stripped.
.TP
.B tc:{session-name}
Send the message body to the named ttychatter session.
.TP
.B tc:{new}
Create a new timestamped session log using the current ttychatter session naming
style, session-YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS.log, under the active SESSION_DIR.
.TP
.B tc:CONFIG
Export or apply the mailbot config attachment.
.TP
.B tc:MODELS
Return the existing MODEL_CACHE_FILE as models-cache.json. This is cache-only;
it does not refresh models.
.TP
.B tc:MODELS TEXT
Search the existing model cache for TEXT. This is also cache-only.
.TP
.B tc:CMD
Run the first nonempty message-body line as a mailbot command.
.TP
.B tc:command args
Run a mailbot command directly from the subject.
.TP
.B MAILBOT
When included in BODY_COMMAND_SUBJECTS, use the first nonempty body line as
the command or session selector. "session NAME" and "chat NAME" route the
remaining body to that chat session.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Return the regular-user email command summary.
.TP
.B help-admin
Return administrator/operator help. Requires ALLOWED_FROM.
.TP
.B manpage
Return this manual as a plain-text email attachment. Aliases: manual,
get-manpage, fetch-manpage.
.TP
.B sessions
List saved sessions. Friendly session-title metadata is displayed when present;
filenames remain stable timestamp or subject/session names.
.TP
.B search TEXT
Search session filenames, friendly titles, and log contents.
.TP
.B search-session SESSION TEXT
Search one session log.
.TP
.B rename-session SESSION TITLE
Set session-title metadata. This no longer renames the log file. Aliases include
retitle-session, title-session, and set-session-title.
.TP
.B rename-session-file OLD NEW
Legacy escape hatch that renames the session log file.
.TP
.B turns SESSION
Run ttychatter --turns for the session.
.TP
.B branch SESSION TURN
Run ttychatter --branch for the session and turn.
.TP
.B export SESSION [markdown|text|json]
Export a session. Markdown is the default. JSON support depends on the selected
backend; the Bash-only ttychatter intentionally omits JSON export.
.TP
.B delete-session SESSION
Delete a session log. Aliases: delete, rm, remove-session, rm-session. The target
must resolve inside SESSION_DIR and the supplied name must already be the exact
sanitized session name.
.TP
.B archive-session [on|off|status]
Show or change the sender's public-mode archive-on-expire preference. Aliases:
archive-opt-in and archive-opt-out.
.TP
.B user
Show this sender's registry id, private HOME, per-user config path, and API-key
source.
.TP
.B prefs
Show this sender's ttychatter configuration. Alias for ttyconfig.
.TP
.B tty-set KEY VALUE
Set an allowlisted per-user ttychatter preference. The allowed list is
USER_TTYCONFIG_ALLOWED_KEYS. Alias: set. The mailbot emits C-compatible
--set KEY=VALUE syntax for the C backend and --set KEY VALUE for the Python and
Bash helpers.
.TP
.B tty-unset KEY
Remove an allowlisted per-user ttychatter preference. Alias: unset.
.TP
.B api-key KEY
Store this sender's persistent OpenRouter API key in USER_SECRET_DIR as a chmod
600 secret file. The key is not written to .config. Aliases include set-api-key,
api-key-persistent, and persistent-api-key. This command is available only when
USER_API_KEY_MODE is persistent or both and ALLOW_USER_API_KEYS=1.
.TP
.B api-key-session KEY
Store this sender's temporary OpenRouter API key in USER_API_KEY_RUNTIME_DIR.
The key expires after USER_API_KEY_TTL_MINUTES and is preferred over a
persistent user key while valid. Aliases include temp-api-key, api-key-temp,
temporary-api-key, and session-api-key. This command is available only when
USER_API_KEY_MODE is session or both and ALLOW_USER_API_KEYS=1.
.TP
.B api-key-status
Show this sender's API-key mode, selected API-key source, persistent-key file
path, and temporary-key expiry status. Secret values are not printed.
.TP
.B forget-api-key
Remove this sender's persistent and temporary OpenRouter API keys and then fall
back according to USER_API_KEY_FALLBACK_TO_OPERATOR.
.TP
.B forget-session-api-key
Remove only this sender's temporary runtime OpenRouter API key.
.TP
.B model-cache
Return the existing MODEL_CACHE_FILE only. Never refreshes the cache.
.TP
.B model-search TEXT
Search the existing model cache only. Never refreshes the cache.
.TP
.B update-models
Explicitly run the selected backend with --update-models, then return the model
cache.
.TP
.B models [FLAGS]
Run the selected backend with --models. Aliases include model-list and
list-models.
.TP
.B routers [FLAGS]
Run the selected backend with --routers.
.TP
.B favorites
Run ttychatter --favorites.
.TP
.B favorite-model MODEL
Run ttychatter --favorite-model MODEL.
.TP
.B unfavorite-model MODEL
Run ttychatter --unfavorite-model MODEL.
.TP
.B test-model MODEL
Run ttychatter --test-model MODEL.
.TP
.B show-memory SESSION
Run ttychatter --show-memory SESSION.
.TP
.B clear-memory SESSION
Run ttychatter --clear-memory SESSION.
.TP
.B ttydoctor
Run ttychatter --doctor.
.TP
.B credits
Run ttychatter --credits.
.SH SAFE MODEL-LIST FLAGS
The mailbot allows only a bounded set of model-list flags through email:
.PP
.RS
.nf
--all
--sort VALUE
--modellist-sort-tokens
--min-input-tokens N
--min-output-tokens N
--hide-preview
--show-preview
--require-tokens
--allow-missing-tokens
--favorites-only
--model-type VALUE
.fi
.RE
.SH PUBLIC DEMO MODE
In public mode, a message without a recognized control subject is treated as an
AI prompt. PUBLIC_SESSION_MODE controls isolation: per-sender, per-message, or
shared. The default is per-sender.
.PP
Public sessions use PUBLIC_SESSION_PREFIX and are cleaned up automatically when
PUBLIC_SESSION_CLEANUP=1. PUBLIC_SESSION_IDLE_HOURS,
PUBLIC_SESSION_TTL_HOURS, and PUBLIC_SESSION_MAX_COUNT control deletion.
PUBLIC_SESSION_MAX_TURNS trims surviving public logs to the most recent
input/output cycles.
.PP
When PUBLIC_SESSION_ARCHIVE_ON_DELETE=1, an expiring public log is emailed to
the recorded sender before local deletion. PUBLIC_SESSION_ARCHIVE_USER_TOGGLE=1
lets public users change their own preference with archive-session on/off.
.SH OUTPUT MODES
COMMAND_OUTPUT_MODE, MODEL_CACHE_OUTPUT, MODEL_SEARCH_OUTPUT,
MODEL_LIST_OUTPUT, SESSIONS_OUTPUT, and CONFIG_OUTPUT accept auto, body, or
attachment. The default is auto globally, with short search/session results in
the body and large cache/config results as attachments.
.SH API-KEY MODES
The mailbot can use an operator/default OpenRouter key, per-user persistent
keys, or per-user temporary runtime keys. The mode is controlled by
USER_API_KEY_MODE.
.TP
.B USER_API_KEY_MODE=operator
Use only DEFAULT_OPENROUTER_API_KEY_FILE or API keys from the mailbot process
environment. User key commands are refused.
.TP
.B USER_API_KEY_MODE=persistent
Allow users to save persistent chmod 600 key files in USER_SECRET_DIR. This is
the compatibility default.
.TP
.B USER_API_KEY_MODE=session
Allow users to save temporary runtime keys with api-key-session. Persistent key
files are not used.
.TP
.B USER_API_KEY_MODE=both
Allow temporary and persistent user keys. Temporary runtime keys take priority,
then persistent user key files, then the operator key if fallback is enabled.
.TP
.B USER_API_KEY_TTL_MINUTES=N
Expiration time for api-key-session keys. The default is 60 minutes.
.TP
.B USER_API_KEY_RUNTIME_DIR=PATH
Directory for temporary runtime key JSON files. The default is
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ttychatter/mailbot/user-api-keys when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is set,
otherwise /tmp/ttychatter-mailbot-UID/user-api-keys. Files are written mode
0600 and parent directories mode 0700.
.TP
.B USER_API_KEY_FALLBACK_TO_OPERATOR=0|1
When enabled, users without a usable user key fall back to the operator/default
OpenRouter key. When disabled, USER_API_KEY_MODE=persistent/session/both require
a user key for that sender. The default is 1 for compatibility.
.PP
Temporary API keys avoid long-term storage under .local/state or .config, but
they are still present in runtime storage while valid and are still exposed to
the mail path unless the user's email is encrypted end-to-end. They do not hide
secrets from a trusted host administrator or root.
.TP
.B API_KEY_COMMANDS_REQUIRE_BODY=0|1
When enabled, api-key, api-key-session, and tty-set API-key commands that
include a secret operand are refused when the secret appears in the subject.
Users should send Subject: tc:CMD and put the secret command in the message
body. The default is 1.
.SH CONFIGURATION KEYS
Important keys include IMAP_HOST, IMAP_PORT, IMAP_SSL, IMAP_USER,
IMAP_PASSWORD, IMAP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE, SEND_METHOD, SENDMAIL_PATH,
MAIL_FROM, MAIL_TO, ALLOWED_FROM, DENY_FROM, BANNED_FROM, BANNED_LIST,
REJECT_SELF_SENDER, SUBJECT_PREFIX, SUBJECT_SEPARATOR, SESSION_OPEN_DELIM,
SESSION_CLOSE_DELIM, BODY_COMMAND_SUBJECTS, ALLOW_COMMANDS_IN_SUBJECT,
ALLOW_BODY_COMMAND_SUBJECTS, ALLOW_BARE_CONTROL_SUBJECTS,
ALLOW_LEGACY_BRACED_CONTROL, RE_SESSION_SUBJECTS, OPEN_TO_PUBLIC,
PUBLIC_SESSION_MODE, PUBLIC_SESSION_PREFIX, PUBLIC_SHARED_SESSION,
PUBLIC_ALLOWED_COMMANDS, PUBLIC_SESSION_CLEANUP, PUBLIC_SESSION_TTL_HOURS,
PUBLIC_SESSION_IDLE_HOURS, PUBLIC_SESSION_MAX_COUNT, PUBLIC_SESSION_MAX_TURNS,
USER_REGISTRY, SUBJECT_SESSIONS, USER_REGISTRY_FILE, USER_HOME_ROOT,
USER_SECRET_DIR, DEFAULT_OPENROUTER_API_KEY_FILE,
MIGRATE_PLAINTEXT_OPENROUTER_API_KEY, ALLOW_USER_API_KEYS,
USER_API_KEY_MODE, API_KEY_MODE, USER_API_KEY_TTL_MINUTES,
USER_API_KEY_RUNTIME_DIR, USER_API_KEY_FALLBACK_TO_OPERATOR,
API_KEY_COMMANDS_REQUIRE_BODY, USER_TTYCONFIG_ALLOWED_KEYS, SPAM_PROTECTION,
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED,
DAILY_QUOTA_ENABLED, MAX_SESSIONS_PER_SENDER, API_COST_PROTECTION,
API_MAX_INPUT_CHARS, API_MAX_ESTIMATED_TOKENS, API_MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES,
TTYCHATTER_BACKEND, TTYCHATTER_CLIENT, TTYCHATTER_COMMAND, TTYCHATTER_EXTRA_ARGS,
AI_FILE_DOWNLOAD_MODE, MAILBOT_SEND_AI_FILES, TTYCHATTER_CONTROL_TIMEOUT, MODEL_CACHE_FILE, SESSION_DIR, ATTACHMENT_DIR,
WORK_DIR, PROCESSED_DB, COMMAND_OUTPUT_MODE, MODEL_CACHE_OUTPUT,
MODEL_SEARCH_OUTPUT, MODEL_LIST_OUTPUT, SESSIONS_OUTPUT, CONFIG_OUTPUT,
OUTPUT_INLINE_MAX_BYTES, MAX_COMMAND_OUTPUT_BYTES, and
MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES.

.SH AI-RETURNED FILE ATTACHMENTS
Current ttychatter backends can record provider-returned file attachments when a
provider exposes downloadable file metadata, data URLs, or base64 payloads in the
chat response. The mailbot is noninteractive, so the safest default is metadata
only unless the operator or user explicitly enables downloading.
.PP
Set AI_FILE_DOWNLOAD_MODE to ask, metadata, auto, or off. In mailbot use, ask
degrades to metadata because there is no terminal prompt. metadata lists returned
files in the reply body without saving them. auto passes --ai-download auto to
the selected ttychatter backend and saves returned files under
ATTACHMENT_DIR/received when possible. off ignores returned file metadata.
.PP
When MAILBOT_SEND_AI_FILES=1, saved returned files located under ATTACHMENT_DIR
are attached to the outgoing email reply, subject to MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES.
Users in registry mode may request downloads with a tty-set command when
USER_TTYCONFIG_ALLOWED_KEYS allows AI_FILE_DOWNLOAD_MODE:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Subject: tc:CMD
tty-set AI_FILE_DOWNLOAD_MODE auto
.fi
.RE

.SH XDG PATHS
Without overrides, ttychatter.mailbot follows the XDG base-directory layout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
config:      $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/config
state:       $XDG_STATE_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/
cache:       $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/
sessions:    $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions/
attachments: $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments/
model cache: $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json
runtime user keys: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ttychatter/mailbot/user-api-keys/
.fi
.RE
.PP
When USER_REGISTRY=1, every sender gets a private HOME under USER_HOME_ROOT.
That HOME contains the same ttychatter OpenRouter config/data/cache layout used
by the C, Python, and Bash clients.
.PP
Compatibility fallback is retained for the older model cache name
models-cache.json and older favorites file model-favorites.txt.
.SH SECURITY
Public mode is for demos. It should use a separate mailbox, conservative limits,
per-sender registry homes, subject sessions, and a small PUBLIC_ALLOWED_COMMANDS
set. Do not expose config mutation, model refresh, session deletion, api-key, api-key-session,
tty-set, or tty-unset to non-ALLOWED_FROM senders unless the deployment is
intentionally disposable.
.PP
OpenRouter keys are loaded according to USER_API_KEY_MODE. They may come from
DEFAULT_OPENROUTER_API_KEY_FILE, a per-user persistent secret file, a temporary
runtime key file, or the mailbot process environment. The selected key is
injected into the ttychatter subprocess environment. The mailbot migrates legacy
plaintext API-key lines out of ttychatter config when
MIGRATE_PLAINTEXT_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=1.
.PP
api-key-session is intended for encrypted-mail or otherwise trusted mail paths.
It avoids long-term storage by expiring keys from runtime storage, but ordinary
email and the server host are not secret from the mail operator/root. Keep
API_KEY_COMMANDS_REQUIRE_BODY=1 so keys are not copied into mail subjects.
.PP
SPAM_PROTECTION rejects auto-submitted/list/bulk mail and recipient floods.
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED enforces rolling sender/global work caps. DAILY_QUOTA_ENABLED
enforces daily sender/global caps. MAX_MESSAGE_BYTES, MAX_ATTACHMENT_COUNT,
MAX_TOTAL_ATTACHMENT_BYTES, MAX_SESSIONS_PER_SENDER, and API_COST_PROTECTION
protect the mail-to-API boundary before ttychatter is called.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/config
Default mailbot config.
.TP
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/processed-ids.txt
Processed-message database.
.TP
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/users.json
User registry.
.TP
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/users/
Per-user HOME roots.
.TP
.B ~/.secrets/ttychatter/mailbot/openrouter-default.key
Default server OpenRouter key.
.TP
.B ~/.secrets/ttychatter/mailbot/openrouter-users/
Per-user persistent OpenRouter keys.
.TP
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ttychatter/mailbot/user-api-keys/
Per-user temporary runtime OpenRouter keys, when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is set.
.TP
.B /tmp/ttychatter-mailbot-UID/user-api-keys/
Fallback temporary runtime OpenRouter key directory when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is not set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success. Nonzero status indicates configuration, IMAP, SMTP,
sendmail, or ttychatter subprocess failure.
